       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. The usual starting dose is 2.5 to 5 mg daily. A 50 mg dose could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Because amlodipine has a long half-life, those effects could last for days.\n\nCan you check the intended dose? Here are some possibilities:\n- **5 mg by mouth once daily**, a typical starting dose.\n- **10 mg by mouth once daily**, the maximum dose.\n- **2.5 mg by mouth once daily**, for frail or elderly patients, or patients with hepatic impairment.\n\nIf 50 mg is really what you want, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter the order right away."
